course: dictionary
lesson: 13938
title: Lens, not lense
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lense is a common misspelling. The correct spelling is lens, with an s at the end. One piece of curved glass is a lens, and more than one is lenses.
explain: A lens is a curved piece of glass or clear plastic that bends light. «She cleaned her glasses with a soft cloth.» Her glasses have lenses in them, so they can help her see clearly.
explain: Lenses are used in cameras, microscopes and your eyes too. «The scientist looked at the tiny ant through a magnifying lens.» The lens made the ant look much bigger.
fact: The correct spelling is lens, not lense.
fact: «Lense» is a common misspelling of «lens».
fact: The plural of lens is lenses: one lens, two lenses.
fact: A convex lens is thicker in the middle and can magnify and focus light.
fact: A concave lens is thinner in the middle and spreads light out.
exercise: «The magnifying lens made the tiny beetle look huge.» Which spelling is correct? | lenz | lense | *lens
exercise: Which word is the correct spelling of the curved glass that bends light? | lenz | lenss | lense | *lens
exercise: «The scientist put two ___ on the table.» Choose the correct word for two of them. | *lenses | lense | lensses | lensis
test: A convex lens is thicker in the middle. What can it do to light? | *It can magnify and focus light | It stops light from passing through | It makes sound louder | It turns light into colour
test: Which is the correct plural of lens? | lensez | *lenses | lense | lensies
exam: Which sentence is spelled correctly? | «The camera lense was dusty.» | «The camera lenss was dusty.» | *«The camera lens was dusty.»
